          title: 'Stargazing in the Wadi',
          text: 'The Ash Sharqiyah region has minimal light pollution and the mountains block coastal haze, making the sky above Wadi Shab exceptional for stargazing. Set up on the flat gravel near the wadi entrance after dark and the Milky Way arcs clearly overhead. The Hajar Mountains silhouetted against the stars and the sound of the falaj channels trickling creates an atmosphere of profound quiet. Bring a blanket and download a star-map app before losing mobile signal.',
          tip: 'New moon nights in the dry season (October–April) offer the darkest skies. The wadi entrance area has a flat gravel car park suitable for laying out a blanket away from headlights.',
